# Generated knowledge-base artifacts (#7935).
#
# These three files are produced by scripts/generate-kb-index.sh and committed.
# Without the entries below git merges them as ordinary prose, so every branch
# that adds a knowledge-base file conflicts with every other one -- and the
# reflex resolution (`git checkout --theirs`) takes one side's copy whole,
# silently discarding the rows the other side added.
#
# INDEX.md carries a derived `> Total files:` header, so `union` is wrong for it:
# two sides that each add the same NUMBER of files write identical count text,
# git merges the line cleanly, and the result is wrong with no conflict and no
# marker. It gets a real three-way driver instead.
#
# The driver is registered as merge.kb-index.driver by
# scripts/install-kb-merge-driver.sh, which runs from SessionStart and from the
# package.json `prepare` lifecycle script. Git gives NO signal when a driver
# named here is unregistered -- it silently falls back to the default text merge
# -- so scripts/generate-kb-index.sh --check is what makes that case loud.
knowledge-base/INDEX.md merge=kb-index

# The facet files are flat sorted lists with no derived header, and their only
# content consumer validates with `grep -Fxq` -- an exact-line check indifferent
# to ordering and duplicates. git's built-in union therefore satisfies the real
# contract with zero code and, being built in, no unregistered-failure mode at
# all. The next generator run restores canonical ordering.
knowledge-base/kb-tags.txt merge=union
knowledge-base/kb-categories.txt merge=union

# NOTE: plugins/soleur/knowledge-base/* is deliberately NOT covered. Nothing in
# this repo writes it -- it is a hand-maintained plugin payload, so there is no
# generator for it to be a pure function of. The patterns above are anchored to
# the root paths and cannot match the mirror.
